5.6 Input and Output Functions
==============================

The following function writes a polynomial to an output stream.  When
using it, you need to include ‘stdio.h’ _before_ ‘mpfrcx.h’.

 -- Function: size_t mpfrx_out_str (FILE* STREAM, int BASE, size_t
          N_DIGITS, mpfrx_srcptr F)
 -- Function: size_t mpcx_out_str (FILE* STREAM, int BASE, size_t
          N_DIGITS, mpcx_srcptr F)

     Output F to STREAM using the given BASE and the given number of
     digits N_DIGITS for the coefficients.  If N_DIGITS is 0, then a
     suitable number of digits is chosen so that reading the polynomial
     into a variable of the same precision as F yields the same
     polynomial again (this input function needs yet to be written...).

     The output starts with an opening bracket ‘'('’, followed by the
     degree and a list of coefficients in decreasing order of degree
     (separated by spaces) and a closing bracket ‘')'’.

     Return the number of written characters.


